  "body": "> Replaces #421, moved to the new fork (the old one left NeoTech's network, and a push there closes the PR). Main is merged in.\n>\n> - **`mcp/mod.rs`:** this PR's `fixture_tools` and `setup_tools` modules sit beside #422's `features` and `pick`.\n> - **`posting.rs`:** #368 added a gate problem for a tool whose modelled body no longer fits it, as a string. This PR had turned the fixture walk into data. `fixture_findings` now returns `FixtureFindings { hits, unjudged }`: the post gate lists both, and `get_fixture_findings` reports `unjudged` and is `ok` only when both are empty, so neither drops the problem.\n>\n> Gate: fixtures, carried_fixtures_cache, rotary_fixtures, verify, setup_sheet, mcp, mcp_setup, posting, tool_body, turning_holder and drilling_cross_holder all pass. `clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## What changed\nNine new MCP tools for the setup furniture. Each write tool runs one existing command through the session History, so undo and redo work, and every refusal comes back as a tool error.\n\n- `add_setup` (CreateSetup, optional `name` / `datum_from`; the new setup becomes active), `activate_setup` (ActivateSetup).\n- `set_wcs` (SetWcsOrigin): an absolute `origin`, or a `stock_point` with min/center/max per axis of the active setup's stock box plus an optional `offset`; optional rotation quaternion `[x,y,z,w]` (omitted keeps the current one).\n- `set_work_offset` (SetSetupWorkOffset): G54-G59 or `null`; refuses on a document with no setups.\n- `load_machine` (LoadMachine, or SetSetupMachine when `setup` is given): exactly one of `builtin`, `path` or `clear`; an unknown name is refused with the list.\n- `add_fixture` / `remove_fixture` / `move_fixture` (TagFixture / UntagFixture / MoveFixture).\n- `get_fixture_findings` (read-only): each setup's fixtures with bounds, the machine table box, and one finding per live collision (`op`, `move`, `kind: \"fixture_hit\"`, `part`, `message`, `blocks_post`). A stale op answers `judged: false` with the reason, never an empty all-clear.\n- `posting.rs`: `fixture_problems` is now a thin wrapper over a new `pub fn fixture_findings(world)`, so the tool and the post gate read one check. Gate strings are unchanged.\n- Registration: new tools live in `mcp/setup_tools.rs` and `mcp/fixture_tools.rs`, chained into the table by an `all()` helper; the existing `TOOLS` array rows are untouched (small conflict surface with the other open MCP PRs).\n\n## Readings\nDebug, M5 Mac: new binary `mcp_setup` 3/3; `mcp` 4, `fixtures` 14, `rotary_fixtures` 4, `axis_direction` 12 all pass. `scripts/gate.sh quick` (all camcraft-app suites): 1290 passed, 1 failed - the known main red `setup_stock_source::a_new_block_after_a_flip_starts_from_its_own_stock_and_undoes` (#415). Clippy `-D warnings` clean.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/mcp_setup.rs`)\n- `g54_off_the_stock_corner_a_machine_and_fixture_findings_as_data` - the issue's done-criterion: G54 at the stock's top front-left corner (checked in `get_job`, undo/redo), \"VMC 3-axis\" loaded, a Face op generated, a vise marked and moved into the pass; findings come back as data and `verify`'s gate fails; undoing the move and unmarking clear them.\n- `setups_declare_activate_and_post_their_own_word`\n- `bad_setup_input_is_a_tool_error`\n\n## Not exercised\n`load_machine` with a real `.mch` path (only the unreadable-path refusal); rotation on `move_fixture`; fixed fixtures (SetFixtureFixed has no tool yet). No GUI change, no posted G-code change.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/181-mcp-setup-tools.md`.\n\nChangelog: MCP tools to declare and activate setups, set the WCS origin and work offset, load a machine, mark and move fixtures, and read fixture findings as data\n\nFixes #181\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
